    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0091" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/303a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d60-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-10T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1918,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7203. Department desires to ascertain what policy adopted by Great Britain in
                    regard to meeting interest and principal on Russian obligations.</p>
                <p>Please report fully as to policy and arrangements made in detail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d60-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d60-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date, to the
                    Ambassador in France (No. 3479).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
